;; Regulatory source register for JPN-JFTC (公正取引委員会, Japan Fair Trade
;; Commission) antitrust and subcontractor-fairness compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: "Every regulatory claim must cite the official JFTC
;; source." Until this file existed there was no such list, so no claim in
;; this repository could be traced to anything. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it.
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be:
;;                   laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app that answers
;;                   HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>, renders "not found"
;;                   client-side, and therefore cannot tell a real citation
;;                   from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; WHY www.jftc.go.jp IS CITED HERE, AGAINST THE repo-INTERNAL facts.cljc.
;; The cljc catalog records that www.jftc.go.jp is "unverified, human-only"
;; because a previous run tripped an automated-client block. Re-measured
;; 2026-08-29 with a current Chrome User-Agent header: a cold client gets
;; real 200 pages, and a nonexistent path answers 404 -- not 403, not a WAF
;; challenge, not a throttled page. The register cites the same host here
;; only for pages this run fetched live, and only on the strength of the
;; title/charset/url it read at the moment of citation. If the host's
;; behaviour changes back, :host-behaviour declares the measured behaviour
;; and the verifier re-measures it on every run.
;;
;; HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path
;; that does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every
;; host in the register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note
;; saying "measured to refuse correctly" degrades into a constant the
;; moment it is written; a declaration the run re-measures cannot.
;;
;; JFTC IS ESTABLISHED BY THE ANTITRUST ACT, NOT BY ITS OWN 設置法.
;; Unlike most Japanese ministries, the JFTC is created by 私的独占の禁止
;; 及び公正取引の確保に関する法律 chapter VIII article 27, and no law whose
;; title is 公正取引委員会設置法 exists on e-Gov. This register therefore
;; carries no `law.jftc-establishment` entry, and that absence is recorded
;; as a :coverage entry below so an operator reading the register knows it
;; is the absence that was looked for, not an oversight.
;;
;; The Antimonopoly Act entry (law.jftc.antimonopoly-act) is the act that
;; BOTH empowers the JFTC to enforce the antitrust regime AND is the
;; statute the JFTC administers to bind private conduct. The two roles are
;; not separated in this register because the law is one.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in an antitrust/subcontract register.
;; Claims stop at the level actually checked -- law identity, and for the
;; page entries the title, URL, charset, and the de-tagged strings read on
;; 2026-08-29. No article text and no PDF is asserted, because none was
;; read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.www-jftc-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.jftc.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "Re-measured 2026-08-29: a cold client gets real 200 pages
                (front page 86522 bytes, title `公正取引委員会`); a nonexistent
                path answers 404 with a 529-byte 404 Not Found page whose
                title is `404 Not Found`. Both responses are served at the
                requested URL with no redirect, so :page-identity and
                :page-text both discriminate. The repo-internal
                src/statute/facts.cljc records an earlier window in which
                the host was 403 to automated clients; that window is not
                what this run measured, and the register is pinned to this
                run's measurement rather than to a memory of a prior one.
                :host/missing-path is :refuses because the path is
                answered with a real status-and-body that is not the page
                asked for; the verifier's :refuses branch reads the status
                and a real body, and 404 in that branch is the same shape
                as METI's 403."}

 {:source/id "host.www-japaneselawtranslation-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "Re-measured 2026-08-29: a cold client gets real 200 pages
                (/laws/ 44458 bytes UTF-8, title `Search by Title - Law
                Search - Japanese Law Translation`); a nonexistent path
                answers 404 with a 1667-byte Error page served at the
                requested URL, with no redirect. Charset is utf-8; the
                title is unique to the page asked for. :refuses because
                the path is answered with a real status-and-body that is
                not the page asked for."}

 ;; ── Coverage of what this register does NOT cite ─────────────────────────

 {:source/id "coverage.jftc"
  :source/kind :coverage
  :coverage/entries 8
  :coverage/by-verify {:e-gov-law-id 5 :page-identity 2 :page-text 1}
  :source/note "5 statutes (one of which is also the act that creates the
                JFTC), 2 :page-identity entries, 1 :page-text entry, and 2
                :host-behaviour entities. No 公正取引委員会設置法 -- the JFTC
                is established by the Antimonopoly Act (law.jftc.antimonopoly-act,
                chapter VIII, article 27), and an operator searching e-Gov
                for a 設置法 finds nothing. That absence is intentional."}

 ;; ── Statutes: the act that BOTH administers the antitrust regime AND
 ;;    establishes the JFTC. Title and law number are exactly what e-Gov
 ;;    returned at retrieval time. Re-verified 2026-08-29. ─────────────────

 {:source/id "law.jftc.antimonopoly-act"
  :source/kind :statute
  :source/title "私的独占の禁止及び公正取引の確保に関する法律"
  :source/publisher "e-Gov 法令検索 (Digital Agency)"
  :source/url "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/322AC0000000054"
  :source/verify :e-gov-law-id
  :egov/law-id "322AC0000000054"
  :egov/law-title "昭和二十二年法律第五十四号（私的独占の禁止及び公正取引の確保に関する法律）"
  :egov/law-num "昭和二十二年法律第五十四号"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:antitrust :cartel :agency-establishment}
  :source/note "The Antimonopoly Act (独占禁止法). Identity only: cartel
                prohibition, private-monopolisation prohibition, unfair-trade-
                practices regulation, merger review, and the surcharge (課徴金)
                regime are article text and are NOT asserted here. Chapter VIII
                article 27 establishes the JFTC; that is the reason a leaf
                repository scoped to one ministry cites the act itself rather
                than a separate establishment act."}

 {:source/id "law.jftc.subcontract-act"
  :source/kind :statute
  :source/title "製造委託等に係る中小受託事業者に対する代金の支払の遅延等の防止に関する法律"
  :source/publisher "e-Gov 法令検索 (Digital Agency)"
  :source/url "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/331AC0000000120"
  :source/verify :e-gov-law-id
  :egov/law-id "331AC0000000120"
  :egov/law-title "製造委託等に係る中小受託事業者に対する代金の支払の遅延等の防止に関する法律"
  :egov/law-num "昭和三十一年法律第百二十号"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:subcontractor-fairness :payment-terms}
  :source/note "Formerly the 下請代金支払遅延等防止法 (Subcontract Act, 下請法),
                RENAMED by 令和七年法律第四十一号 effective 2026-01-01 to its
                current title (often abbreviated 取適法). Operator-facing JFTC
                material may still say 下請法; the law number 昭和三十一年法律
                第百二十号 is the stable handle. The title carried here is what
                e-Gov returns at retrieval time -- not the customary name."}

 {:source/id "law.jftc.bid-rigging-involvement-act"
  :source/kind :statute
  :source/title "入札談合等関与行為の排除及び防止並びに職員による入札等の公正を害すべき行為の処罰に関する法律"
  :source/publisher "e-Gov 法令検索 (Digital Agency)"
  :source/url "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/414AC1000000101"
  :source/verify :e-gov-law-id
  :egov/law-id "414AC1000000101"
  :egov/law-title "入札談合等関与行為の排除及び防止並びに職員による入札等の公正を害すべき行為の処罰に関する法律"
  :egov/law-num "平成十四年法律第百一号"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:bid-rigging-prevention :public-procurement}
  :source/note "官製談合防止法, the bid-rigging-facilitation-by-public-officials
                statute. The act is on the books because the Antimonopoly Act
                addresses private bid-rigging and a separate instrument was
                needed for situations in which a public officer is the actor.
                Identity only; the criminal-liability scope and the
                bid-suspension regime that follows from a conviction are not
                asserted."}

 {:source/id "law.jftc.freelance-act"
  :source/kind :statute
  :source/title "特定受託事業者に係る取引の適正化等に関する法律"
  :source/publisher "e-Gov 法令検索 (Digital Agency)"
  :source/url "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/505AC0000000025"
  :source/verify :e-gov-law-id
  :egov/law-id "505AC0000000025"
  :egov/law-title "特定受託事業者に係る取引の適正化等に関する法律"
  :egov/law-num "令和五年法律第二十五号"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:subcontractor-fairness :freelance}
  :source/note "フリーランス法 / 事業者間取引適正化等法. Newest JFTC-
                administered trade-fairness act, effective 2024-11-01. The
                register's customary name フリーランス法 does not appear in the
                title e-Gov holds; the full e-Gov title is what is recorded."}

 {:source/id "law.jftc.secretariat-organization-order"
  :source/kind :statute
  :source/title "公正取引委員会事務総局組織令"
  :source/publisher "e-Gov 法令検索 (Digital Agency)"
  :source/url "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/327CO0000000373"
  :source/verify :e-gov-law-id
  :egov/law-id "327CO0000000373"
  :egov/law-title "公正取引委員会事務総局組織令"
  :egov/law-num "昭和二十七年政令第三百七十三号"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:agency-organization}
  :source/note "Cabinet Order organising the JFTC General Secretariat -- the
                instrument that, alongside the Antimonopoly Act, gives the
                agency its internal shape. Identity only: the bureaux and
                divisions the order establishes are article text and are NOT
                asserted."}

 ;; ── Pages on the JFTC host: citable because this run fetched them live ──

 {:source/id "page.jftc.home"
  :source/kind :page
  :source/title "公正取引委員会"
  :source/publisher "公正取引委員会 (JFTC)"
  :source/url "https://www.jftc.go.jp/"
  :page/title "公正取引委員会"
  :source/verify :page-identity
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-08-29"
  :source/covers #{:agency-landing}
  :source/note "JFTC front page. 86522 bytes UTF-8 (the default charset when
                the register does not declare one), served at the requested
                URL with no redirect. Title is the agency's institutional name
                -- the same string appears inside the body, and a verifier
                reading either discriminates the same way. Charset is left
                undeclared so the entry joins the verifier's :page-identity
